# No AI / Cursor attribution in commits or PRs

When creating git commits or pull requests for this project:

- Do **not** mention Cursor, Cursor Agent, Auto, Composer, Copilot, ChatGPT, Claude, or any other AI/assistant tool or product name.
- Do **not** write phrases like "Generated with Cursor", "Co-authored-by: Cursor", "AI-assisted", "agent implemented", or similar attribution.
- Do **not** add AI tool footers, badges, or trailers to commit messages or PR bodies.
- Write commit messages and PR titles/bodies as a normal human teammate would: focus on **why** the change matters and what it does for the product.

```text
❌ BAD
Add LexAtlas auth UI

Generated with Cursor Agent
Co-Authored-By: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

✅ GOOD
Add LexAtlas auth UI with login, register, and password reset
```

```text
❌ BAD
## Summary
- Implemented by Cursor agent from Figma

## Test plan
- …
```

```text
✅ GOOD
## Summary
- Add LexAtlas auth screens matching the product design
- Support attorney verification pending admin approval

## Test plan
- …
```
